@startuml logic-update-pipeline
title UniChat — Auto-update pipeline (reference logic from master)

participant "UI (settings/about page)" as UI
participant "update.command" as CMD
participant "update-api.service.rs" as API
participant "update-downloader.service.rs" as DL
participant "update-installer.service.rs" as INS
participant "update-platform.service.rs" as PLAT
participant "GitHub Releases API" as GH

UI -> CMD: get_current_version()
CMD --> UI: VersionInfo (compile-time version)

UI -> CMD: check_for_update()
API -> GH: GET /repos/<owner>/<repo>/releases/latest
GH --> API: GitHubRelease{ tag_name, assets[] }
API -> API: find_platform_asset(assets)\n- Platform from update-platform.service\n  (os + arch + target triple)\n- has_matching_extension: .exe/.msi (win),\n  .app/.dmg (mac), .AppImage/.deb (linux),\n  .apk (android)
alt newer than current
  API --> UI: UpdateInfo{ version, notes, asset url }
else up to date
  API --> UI: None
end

UI -> CMD: download_update(version)
DL -> GH: stream asset to temp path\n(get_temp_download_path)
DL -->> UI: DownloadProgress{ bytes, total } events

UI -> CMD: install_update()
INS -> INS: verify downloaded artifact,\nlaunch platform installer / replace binary
note right: app exits; installer takes over

Failure rules (master):
- no matching asset for platform -> error surfaced to UI
- partial download -> temp file discarded, retry safe
- checksum/signature mismatch -> install aborted

note over CMD: dioxus-migration status: handlers exist but return None/success;\nno GitHub query, no progress channel, no installer.
@enduml
